---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JourneyMap from '../../components/JourneyMap.astro';
import JourneyTimeline from '../../components/JourneyTimeline.astro';
import MikaCurrentPin from '../../components/MikaCurrentPin.astro';
import OpenQuestions from '../../components/OpenQuestions.astro';
import { mikaJourney, validateJourneyState } from '../../data/journey';
import { parseLearningLogDate, sortJourneyEntries } from '../../lib/journey-timeline';

const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;
const journeyErrors = validateJourneyState(mikaJourney);
if (journeyErrors.length) throw new Error(`Invalid Journey state:\n${journeyErrors.join('\n')}`);

const entries = sortJourneyEntries(
  (await getCollection('notes', ({ data }) => !data.draft))
    .filter((note) => note.id.startsWith('learning-log-'))
).map((entry) => ({
  id: entry.id,
  title: entry.data.title,
  description: entry.data.description,
  topic: entry.data.topic,
  href: `${base}notes/${entry.id}/`,
  date: parseLearningLogDate(entry.id),
}));
---
<BaseLayout title="Learning journey" description="Mika's public learning frontier and chronological self-taught developer journey.">
  <section class="journey-intro">
    <p class="kicker">learning in public</p>
    <h2>The journey</h2>
    <p>The roadmap is organized knowledge. This is the messy chronological version: what I built, what confused me, what broke, what finally clicked, and what I decided to learn next.</p>
    <p><strong>You are not behind.</strong> I'm still on the map too. My position is public so another self-taught developer can see that the person maintaining this resource is still learning, revisiting fundamentals, and carrying open questions.</p>
  </section>

  <JourneyMap state={mikaJourney} />
  <MikaCurrentPin state={mikaJourney} />

  <JourneyTimeline entries={entries} />

  <OpenQuestions questions={mikaJourney.currentQuestions} />

  <section class="journey-method">
    <p class="kicker">how this becomes a resource</p>
    <h2>Journal first, extract the lesson second</h2>
    <p>A dated entry captures context. A field note captures the reusable idea. A project shows where the idea survived contact with reality. The roadmap connects those pieces so another self-taught developer can use them without having to copy my exact path.</p>
    <p><strong>Learning log → Field note → Project evidence → Roadmap.</strong></p>
    <p><a href={`${base}roadmap/`}>open the roadmap →</a> · <a href={`${base}projects/`}>see the projects →</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
